div.p:
Sings. No more dams I'll make for fish;
                     Nor fetch in firing, at requiring;
                     Nor scrape trencher, nor wash dish:
                     Ban, ban, Ca-caliban,
                     Has a new master, get a new man.

Murder. There long they could not stay;
                     Down the steep hill they run;
                     And to perfect the mischief which they had begun,
                     To murder they bent all their way.

Chorus
{Tie up the winds, and we'll obey;
of  Trit. {Upon the floods we'll sing and play,  & Ner.{And celebrate a Halcyon day.  [Here the Dancers mingle with the Singers, and perform a dance.

Nakar. They muster, they muster, like gnats in the air:
                     Alas! I must leave thee, my fair;
                     And to my light horse-men repair.

Dam. O stay, for you need not to fear them to-night;
                     The wind is for us, and blows full in their sight:
                     And o'er the wide ocean we fight!
                     Like leaves in the autumn our foes will fall down;
                     And hiss in the water.
